      "an_earth_sized_planet_around_a_red_dwa": "An Earth-sized planet around a red dwarf (R ≈ 0.15 Sun radii): depth ~0.37%. Easily detectable. This is why most habitable-zone Earth-sized exoplanets we know orbit red dwarfs.",
      "an_earth_sized_planet_around_a_sun_siz": "An Earth-sized planet around a Sun-sized star: depth ~0.0084% (84 ppm). Kepler detected, ground-based cannot.",
