      "a_antecedent_b_behavior_c_consequence_": "A (Antecedent) → B (Behavior) → C (Consequence). Also called the \"ABC\" of behavior analysis.",
      "a_behavior_can_have_more_than_one_func": "A behavior can have more than one function in reality. For these vignettes, pick the most-likely primary function based on the contingency described.",
      "a_behavior_chain_links_multiple_behavi": "A behavior chain links multiple behaviors in a specific sequence. The completion of one step becomes the signal (SD) for the next. Teach the mouse this chain: Sniff ➜ Rear Up ➜ Press Lever. Reinforce ONLY when the full 3-step chain is completed!",
