      "six_body_plans_one_phylogeny_all_moder": "Six body plans, one phylogeny. All modern cephalopods trace back to the same ~500-million-year-old Cambrian ancestor. The differences between a 6-meter Ordovician sea-monster and a 12-centimeter blue-ringed octopus are differences in evolutionary pressure, not in fundamental architecture.",
