      "a_bat_colony_hangs_on_the_ceiling": "A bat colony hangs on the ceiling",
      "a_bat_s_echolocation_strategy_changes_": "A bat's echolocation strategy changes dramatically during a hunt. Scientists divide the attack into three phases based on pulse rate:",
      "a_d_steer": "⬅️➡️ A/D: Steer",
      "a_moth_is_moving_based_on_the_wave_pat": "A moth is moving. Based on the wave pattern, which direction is it going?",
      "a_rare_luna_moth_hides_in_the_hidden_c": "A rare Luna Moth hides in the hidden chamber",
      "a_single_bat_box_can_house_50_200_bats": "A single bat box can house 50-200 bats. Those bats will eat millions of insects each summer, naturally reducing mosquitoes and crop pests in your area. Science + engineering + conservation = win!",
      "a_single_colony_of_150_big_brown_bats_": "A single colony of 150 big brown bats eats enough cucumber beetles to prevent 33 million rootworm larvae per summer. US bats save farmers $23 billion annually in avoided pesticide costs.",
      "acoustic_ecologists_record_soundscapes": "Acoustic ecologists record soundscapes year-round at fixed locations. By comparing recordings over years, they can detect biodiversity changes — a \"quieter\" spring chorus may indicate declining bird populations.",
      "acoustic_ecology": "Acoustic Ecology",
      "acoustic_ecology_a_soundscape_we_can_t": "Acoustic Ecology — a soundscape we can’t hear",
      "acoustic_niche_hypothesis": "🎵 Acoustic Niche Hypothesis",
      "add_object": "+ Add Object",
      "add_object_to_custom_scene": "Add object to custom scene",
      "adjust_call_frequency_duration_and_ban": "Adjust call frequency, duration, and bandwidth and watch how detection range trades off against resolution. An open exploration — no score, no single right answer.",
      "adjust_min_max_frequency_and_sweep_dur": "Adjust min/max frequency and sweep duration. Widget classifies call type into 4 discrete categories used by real bats. No score, no reveal.",
      "ai_sound_map_generator": "AI Sound Map Generator",
      "air_friction_slows_you_down_over_time": "Air friction slows you down over time",
      "almost_invisible_no_echo": "Almost invisible (no echo)",
      "ambulance_siren": "Ambulance Siren",
      "animals_evolved_to_call_at_different_f": "Animals evolved to call at different frequencies so they don't interfere with each other — like radio stations on different channels. Insects use high frequencies, frogs use mid-range, owls use low frequencies, and bats use ultrasonic frequencies above human hearing. This frequency partitioning allows multiple species to communicate simultaneously without \"jamming\" each other's signals.",
      "annual_value_of_pest_control": "annual value of pest control",
      "arctic_tundra": "Arctic Tundra",
      "as_a_bat_closes_in_on_prey_it_increase": "As a bat closes in on prey, it increases pulse rate from ~10/sec to 200/sec. The Doppler shift of each echo tells the bat exactly how fast the moth is moving.",
      "assistive_technology": "Assistive Technology",
      "at_0_energy_you_can_only_glide_downwar": "At 0% energy, you can only glide downward",
      "at_least_24_tall_x_14_wide_x_3_5_deep_": "At least 24\" tall x 14\" wide x 3.5\" deep. Internal chambers with 3/4\" spacing. Rough or grooved interior surfaces so bats can grip.",
      "audible": "← Audible →",
