      "navigation_v2_content": "Modern navigation uses GPS, but the fundamentals haven't changed: heading (compass direction), airspeed, altitude, and time. Great circle routes (the shortest path between two points on a sphere) appear curved on flat maps but are actually straight on a globe. That's why flights from the US West Coast to Europe often pass over Greenland!",
