      "answer_an_index_fossil_is_a_fossil_spe": "Answer: An index fossil is a fossil species that lived during a specific, limited time period and was geographically widespread. Examples include trilobites, ammonites, and graptolites. They help correlate rocks of the same age.",
      "answer_an_index_fossil_is_a_fossil_spe_2": "Answer: An index fossil is a fossil species that lived during a specific, limited time period and was geographically widespread. Examples include trilobites, ammonites, and graptolites. They help correlate rocks of the same age.",
      "answer_an_index_fossil_is_a_fossil_spe_3": "Answer: An index fossil is a fossil species that lived during a specific, limited time period and was geographically widespread. Examples include trilobites, ammonites, and graptolites. They help correlate rocks of the same age.",
