      "all_season_tires_lose_roughly_40_of_th": "All-season rubber gets stiff in the cold and loses grip. Winter tires use softer rubber that stays flexible, so they grip better on snow, ice and cold pavement. A common rule of thumb is to switch when days stay below about 45°F (7°C). That is well above freezing. Maine law allows studded tires from October 2 to April 30 (29-A §1919).",
