      "brake_hard_let_up_just_before_impact_h": "Brake hard and steer STRAIGHT — do not swerve. Let up on the brake just before impact: the nose rises, which can keep the body from riding up the hood. Aim for where the moose has been, not where it is. Then duck low and toward your DOOR — the door frame is far stronger than the middle of the roof, which is what collapses when a moose comes through.",
