      "most_crashes_are_i_didn_t_see_them": "Most crashes are \"I didn't see them\"",
      "most_drivers_set_side_mirrors_to_see_t": "Most drivers set side mirrors to see the back of their own car — that doubles the rearview mirror. Instead: LEAN LEFT until your head almost touches the window, then adjust the left mirror until you just see your car's side. Repeat on the right by leaning right. When sitting normally, you'll see the lanes beside you — REDUCING BLIND SPOTS. Always look over your shoulder too.",
      "motorcycles_and_bicycles_can_hide_in_b": "• Motorcycles and bicycles can hide in blind spots that even cars cannot.",
      "motorcycles_fit_entirely_in_your_a_pil": "Motorcycles fit ENTIRELY in your A-pillar blind spot (the pillar between windshield and door). Bikes + cyclists do the same. Always lean to see past pillars at intersections.",
