      "impact_melt_glass": "Impact Melt Glass",
      "in_1610_galileo_observed_venus_through": "In 1610 Galileo observed Venus through his telescope and saw it went through phases — like the Moon. This was proof Venus orbits the Sun, not Earth. Ptolemy's geocentric system can't explain a full Venus. Major evidence for Copernican heliocentrism.",
      "in_1995_hubble_pointed_at_a_tiny_dark_": "In 1995, Hubble pointed at a tiny dark patch of sky for 10 days. Result: 3000 distant galaxies in one image. JWST has now pushed this deeper, finding galaxies just 300 million years after the Big Bang.",
      "in_2006_the_international_astronomical": "In 2006, the International Astronomical Union defined three criteria for a planet: (1) Orbits the Sun ✓, (2) Has enough mass for round shape ✓, (3) Has \"cleared its orbit\" of other debris ✗. Pluto shares its orbital zone with thousands of Kuiper Belt objects, so it’s classified as a \"dwarf planet.\" This doesn’t make it less interesting — New Horizons revealed it’s geologically active!",
