      "detects_internal_defects_measures_dept": "Detects internal defects + measures depth + size. Sensitive (can find very small defects). Portable. Real-time results. Safe (no radiation).",
      "diagnostic_judgment": "Diagnostic judgment: ",
      "diagonal_of_a_3_ft_4_ft_rectangle_3_4_": "Diagonal of a 3 ft × 4 ft rectangle = √(3² + 4²) = √25 = 5 ft. Square check: a frame that measures 3×4 should diagonal exactly 5 (or 5'-0\").",
      "diego_r": "Diego R.",
      "difficulty_tier": "Difficulty Tier",
      "difficulty_tier_2": "Difficulty tier",
      "direct_burns_from_spatter_hot_metal_ar": "Direct burns from spatter + hot metal are the most common acute injury in welding. UV burns (\"sunburn under your shirt\") accumulate over a shift. Long-term skin cancer risk for unprotected welders is elevated 2-4× general population.",
      "discussion": "Discussion",
      "discussion_questions": "Discussion Questions",
      "doubling_rule": "💡 Doubling rule",
      "downhill": "⬇ DOWNHILL",
      "downhill_is_faster_easier_but_provides": "Downhill is FASTER + EASIER but provides LESS penetration. Welders new to pipe often default to downhill, get acceptable visual appearance, but fail X-ray due to lack of fusion at the root. Code-required uphill is uphill for a reason. Check your WPS.",
      "drag_to_orbit": "🖱 Drag to orbit",
      "drawing_number_revision_letter_a_b_c_d": "Drawing number, revision letter (A, B, C...), date, drawn-by, checked-by, scale, material specification, weight. ALWAYS check revision letter — old prints have killed parts.",
      "dual_arm_cobot_for_assembly_delicate_w": "Dual-arm cobot for assembly + delicate work. Less commonly used for welding but emerging.",
      "during_solidification_while_metal_is_s": "During solidification, while metal is still partially molten. Cracks appear immediately after welding.",
      "e6010_deep_penetration_fast_freeze": "E6010 (deep penetration, fast freeze).",
      "e6011_works_on_any_machine_dirty_metal": "E6011 (works on any machine, dirty metal OK).",
      "e6013_smooth_low_penetration": "E6013 (smooth, low penetration).",
      "e7018_low_hydrogen_smooth_bead_aws_req": "E7018 (low hydrogen, smooth bead, AWS-required).",
      "e7024_drag_rod_speed": "E7024 (drag-rod speed).",
      "e70_18": "E70 18",
      "e8018_b2_or_higher_with_preheat_low_hy": "E8018-B2 or higher with preheat + low-hydrogen practice.",
      "each_row_scored_1_5_more_dots_more_of_": "Each row scored 1-5. More dots = more of that attribute.",
      "earn_while_you_learn_registered_appren": "Earn while you learn. Registered apprenticeships at unions (Iron Workers Local 7), at shops (Cianbro, BIW), or via Maine Apprenticeship Program (state-registered). Paid wages from day one, escalating as you certify.",
      "earning_while_learning_no_tuition_full": "Earning while learning. No tuition. Full healthcare from day 1.",
      "eastern_maine_community_college_emcc_b": "Eastern Maine Community College (EMCC, Bangor)",
      "eastern_maine_community_college_emcc_i": "Eastern Maine Community College (EMCC) in Bangor offers a 2-year Welding Technology AAS program (and a shorter 1-year certificate). Hands-on shop time, AWS certification testing built in. Pell-eligible.",
      "eastern_maine_community_college_weldin": "Eastern Maine Community College welding program (Bangor). 2-year associate. BIW actively recruits EMCC grads. Tuition ~$3,500/yr — Maine residents get further discount.",
