      "your_top_matches": "🎯 Your top matches",
      "yumi_abb": "YuMi (ABB)",
      "zumwalts": "Zumwalts",
      "sr_module_explored": "ម៉ូឌុលដែលបានស្វែងយល់៖ {value1}",
      "a11y_score_out_of": "ពិន្ទុ៖ {value1} ក្នុងចំណោម {value2}",
      "sr_quiz_reset": "បានកំណត់សំណួរឡើងវិញ",
      "sr_loaded": "បានផ្ទុក {value1}",
      "sr_showing": "កំពុងបង្ហាញ {value1}",
      "sr_not_quite_see_the_explanation": "មិនទាន់ត្រូវទេ៖ មើលការពន្យល់។",
      "10_real_world_welding_scenarios_for_ea_r2": "10 real-world welding jobs. First tap the clues that decide the process (material, thickness, position, wind, rust, volume), then pick from MIG / TIG / Stick / FCAW / Resistance. Feedback shows what each clue rules in or out, why your pick fits or fails, and reviews your misses at the end.",
      "10_real_world_welding_scenarios_for_ea_r3": "Collect the clues that decide ten welding jobs, then choose a process. After answering, inspect each clue across six processes: see what it supports, argues against or rules out, and which details are neutral. Read why your pick fits or fails and review missed cases.",
      "150_multiple_choice_questions_welding__r2": "Closed book. 150 multiple-choice questions: welding processes, metallurgy, weld design, distortion + residual stress, weld + base metal discontinuities, destructive + non-destructive examination, joint design, welding symbols, basic codes + standards.",
      "3_for_part_c_practice_with_the_actual__r2": "3. For Part C: practise with the same code edition your exam uses. Learn its layout and time yourself looking things up (check the current AWS rules on tabs and notes).",
      "46_multiple_choice_visual_inspection_o_r2": "Hands-on. Measure plastic replicas of real welds with inspection gauges, identify discontinuities, and apply the acceptance criteria in the Book of Specifications supplied with the exam. The Inspector's Bench tab practises this skill.",
      "50_fc_foot_candles_minimum_per_aws_b5__r2": "Required by the governing code. Many shops work to at least 50 fc (foot-candles, about 540 lux) at the weld, and some codes set a higher minimum (ASME Section V, Article 9, for example). A flashlight held at a low angle shows surface texture.",
      "5_joints_4_positions_r2": "5 joints, 5 edge preps, 10 positions",
      "60_multiple_choice_based_on_a_code_boo_r2": "Open code book. Multiple-choice questions on finding and applying provisions of the code chosen at registration (for example AWS D1.1 or API 1104). Speed at navigating the book matters.",
      "6_500_largest_maine_private_employer_r2": "~6,500 (one of the largest private employers in Maine)",
      "6g_position_with_a_metal_ring_placed_a_r2": "The 6G position plus a restriction ring fixed close to the joint, blocking your electrode angle on one side like the brace of a branch connection. Under AWS D1.1 it is the test that qualifies CJP T-, K- and Y-connections in tubular structures (offshore platforms, towers, trusses).",
      "6gr_restricted_6g_with_backing_ring_r2": "6GR — 6G with a restriction ring",
      "a_sealed_pressurized_chamber_called_a__r2": "A sealed pressurized chamber (called a \"habitat\") is placed around the joint and the water is pushed out with gas: air in shallow work, a breathable helium-oxygen mix (heliox) at saturation depths. The diver enters the dry habitat and welds in gas, not water, usually GTAW (TIG) for code-quality results, with argon only as the shielding gas at the torch. Used for permanent repairs on pipelines, oil rig riser sections, and ship hulls.",
      "above_1340_f_face_centered_cubic_cryst_r2": "Stable above the A3 line: about {value1} °F ({value2} °C) for 0.20 % carbon steel, falling to {value3} °F ({value4} °C) at 0.77 % carbon. Between A1 and A3 it shares the steel with ferrite. Face-centered cubic crystal. Dissolves carbon readily. Non-magnetic. Very ductile.",
      "all_modules_live_r2": "All {value1} modules live. From heat-input physics to AWS welding symbols to Maine welding careers, plus the underwater specialty and the Live Bead Run: follow the learning path or explore in any order.",
      "all_positions_2_horizontal_flat_only_4_r2": "= Position: 1 = all positions; 2 = flat and horizontal fillets only; 4 = flat, horizontal, overhead and vertical-down",
      "alternating_current_tig_includes_a_cle_r2": "AC TIG alternates electrode-positive (EP) and electrode-negative (EN) periods. EP provides cathodic cleaning that removes surface oxide; EN puts more heat into the workpiece. A bright etched zone can be visible beside the weld. Standard DCEN TIG does not provide this EP cleaning action.",
      "aluminum_conducts_heat_2_4_faster_than_r2": "Aluminum 6061 conducts heat roughly 3-4× faster than mild steel (about 167 vs 50 W/m·K) and about 10× faster than stainless. The heat you put in spreads out instead of staying at the joint, so you need more amperage for the same thickness (and often preheat on thick sections), and you travel faster before the heat spreads and distorts the part. (The Bead Lab's spreading factor of {value1} for aluminum is a tuned bead-shape number, not this conductivity ratio.)",
      "annual_37_46k_learning_real_world_weld_r2": "Annual {value1}. Learning real-world welding speed + variety.",
      "annual_46_54k_considering_whether_to_s_r2": "Annual {value1}. Considering whether to stay long-term or move on.",
      "annual_46_54k_most_yards_include_healt_r2": "Annual {value1}. Most yards include healthcare. Some bonus on yacht delivery.",
      "annual_70_80k_pension_begins_vesting_a_r2": "Annual ~$70-80K. Pension service is adding up, but nothing is vested yet: you vest at 5 years of service (Year 5).",
      "approximately_50_65_pass_on_first_atte_r2": "Many candidates do not pass every part on the first attempt, and retaking a single part is common. Part C trips up candidates who have never navigated a code book against the clock. ~$1,150 fee per exam attempt. Prep seminars cost extra but are widely recommended.",
