      "arc_xs_v3": "about {value1} past the fusion line: never melted, but its grain changed (representative)",
      "arc_xs_v4": "70% of thickness = {value1}",
      "arc_xs_v5": "{value1} thick: {value2}",
      "bath_iron_works_hires_hundreds_of_weld_r2": "Bath Iron Works hires hundreds of welders a year for US Navy destroyer construction. Cianbro, regional marine yards, paper mills, and pipeline contractors all post welding openings. AWS D1.1 certification + a high-school diploma can land a job paying about {value1} ({value2} a year before overtime) at age 19. A 6G pipe cert plus experience moves you toward {value3} ({value4}). No four-year degree required.",
      "below_1340_f_body_centered_cubic_low_c_r2": "Forms below A3; below A1 ({value1} °F / {value2} °C) it is the stable phase alongside cementite. Body-centered cubic. Holds very little carbon (at most about 0.022 %). Magnetic below about 1418 °F (770 °C). Soft + ductile.",
      "biw_a_general_dynamics_company_builds__r2": "BIW (a General Dynamics company) builds Arleigh Burke-class destroyers (DDG-51) for the US Navy. Founded 1884. Located on the Kennebec River in Bath. One of the largest private employers in Maine.",
      "bl_next_aria": "Related WeldLab modules",
      "bl_next_heat": "The formula behind the bead: Heat Input →",
      "bl_next_hunt": "Spot these defects on real joints: Defect Hunt →",
      "bl_next_met": "What the heat does inside: Metallurgy →",
      "bl_next_run": "Hold it in spec under pressure: Live Bead Run →",
      "bl_next_title": "Keep going",
      "bridge_cam_cambridge_or_fillet_gauge_m_r2": "A Bridge Cam (Cambridge) gauge or a set of fillet weld gauges. They measure reinforcement, undercut depth, fillet leg size and throat.",
      "butt_lap_corner_edge_t_joint_position__r2": "Butt, lap, T, corner and edge joints in cross-section and 3/4 view, with the five butt-joint edge preparations. AWS positions 1G-4G and 1F-4F as pictures with the torch and gravity, plus 5G and 6G pipe. Quiz: spot each joint turned, mirrored, welded a different way or in a 3/4 view.",
      "butt_lap_corner_edge_t_joint_position__r3": "Separate the plates, fit them together and inspect weld locations in five joint configurations. Explore five butt preparations, cross-sections, 3/4 views and welding positions, then identify turned and mirrored joints in the quiz.",
      "car2_chart_aria": "Line chart of cumulative net earnings from age 18 to 40 for three paths. At 25: apprenticeship {value1}, college program {value2}, 4-year degree {value3}. At 40: {value4}, {value5} and {value6}. Crossing points are listed under the chart.",
      "car2_chart_caption": "Ages run along the bottom; height is the running total of pay minus loan payments, in dollars. Dashed guides mark ages 25 and 35. Lettered diamonds mark where two lines cross.",
