      "car2_lad_some": "{value1} of {value2} are in the right place. Look at these pairs:",
      "car2_lad_t1_how": "Walk in to a shop, ask for a helper position. Many shops hire on attitude + willingness to learn.",
      "car2_lad_t1_time": "Day 1",
      "car2_lad_t1_what": "No certification yet. Tack-welding, fit-up, grinding, shop helper duties. Learning by watching.",
      "car2_lad_t2_how": "Complete a trade-school welding program (e.g. EMCC) OR self-study + take certification test at an accredited test facility (~$300-600 test fee).",
      "car2_lad_t2_time": "6-12 months training",
      "car2_lad_t2_what": "Certified to weld structural steel per AWS D1.1 code. Most common entry-level cert — passes you into shipyards, fab shops, ironwork. The plate test is usually 3G + 4G; passing both covers every plate position.",
      "car2_lad_t3_how": "Practice 6G under instruction (most welders take a 1-2 month dedicated prep course). Test at AWS-accredited facility.",
      "car2_lad_t3_time": "1-3 years experience + cert",
      "car2_lad_t3_what": "6G = pipe fixed at 45°, welded with TIG (GTAW — the same process under its AWS name), stick (SMAW) or both, often a TIG root with stick fill. Hardest common position. Opens doors to pipeline, refinery, food-grade stainless, aerospace tier-2.",
      "car2_lad_t4_how": "Pass AWS CWI exam (3-part: fundamentals, practical, code). Required: 5y experience OR formal welding education + experience. ~$1,150 exam fee.",
      "car2_lad_t4_time": "5+ years welding experience + AWS exam",
      "car2_lad_t4_what": "Certified Welding Inspector. Reads prints, inspects welds, signs off on code-compliant work. Office + field hybrid. Very stable career.",
      "car2_lad_t5_how": "Underwater: commercial dive school + AWS underwater cert ($20-30K school cost). Aerospace: experience + specific D17.1/D17.2 testing. Nuclear: company-sponsored qualification.",
      "car2_lad_t5_time": "5+ years + niche certs",
      "car2_lad_t5_what": "Underwater commercial diver-welder, aerospace D17.1, nuclear N509, military shipyard. Highest pay; specialized credentials and physical demands.",
      "car2_lad_title": "Sequencing task: put the credentials in a realistic order",
      "car2_lad_up": "Move {value1} up",
      "car2_lq_6g": "Pipe 6G cert (ASME IX or API 1104)",
      "car2_lq_6g_h": "Pipe fixed at 45°: every position in one joint",
      "car2_lq_6g_w": "Pipe comes after plate: a 6G coupon makes you weld flat, vertical and overhead around one joint, so welders usually reach it after 1-3 years on plate.",
      "car2_lq_cwi": "CWI — Certified Welding Inspector",
      "car2_lq_cwi_h": "Pass the 3-part AWS exam",
      "car2_lq_cwi_w": "You can only sit the 3-part exam (fundamentals, hands-on, code book; {value1} fee) once you are eligible, so the CWI follows eligibility.",
      "car2_lq_d11": "AWS D1.1 structural plate cert (3G + 4G)",
      "car2_lq_d11_h": "The cert most first jobs ask for",
      "car2_lq_d11_w": "Plate comes before pipe: the plate tests take one position at a time, and passing 3G and 4G together covers every plate position. Most first jobs hire on it.",
      "car2_lq_elig": "CWI eligibility (years of work experience)",
      "car2_lq_elig_h": "Documented welding work, not a test",
      "car2_lq_elig_w": "AWS QC1 asks for work experience before you may sit the CWI exam: {value1} years with a high-school diploma, or {value2} with an associate degree in welding technology. Those years are spent welding, so eligibility comes after the welding certs.",
      "car2_lq_scwi": "SCWI — Senior Certified Welding Inspector",
      "car2_lq_scwi_h": "The senior inspector credential",
      "car2_lq_scwi_w": "SCWI is for people who have already worked as CWIs for years, so it comes last. Check AWS QC1 for the current experience rule.",
      "car2_lq_sense": "AWS SENSE entry welder (school or CTE)",
      "car2_lq_sense_h": "Earned in a training program, before a first job",
      "car2_lq_sense_w": "It is the training-stage credential: AWS SENSE (Schools Excelling through National Skills Education) is the standard many CTE and college welding classes test you under, before any employer does.",
      "car2_me_age": "age {value1}",
      "car2_me_appr_cost": "FREE + paid wages (start at about 50% of the journey rate, rising every year; UA Local 716 year 1 is about $22-26/hr)",
      "car2_me_appr_len": "3-5 years (UA pipefitters: 5)",
      "car2_me_best": "Highest in this table: {value1} ({value2} + {value3}). Lowest: {value4} ({value5} + {value6}). Read the trade-offs before you chase the top number.",
      "car2_me_biw_emcc": "EMCC welding program (1-yr certificate or 2-yr associate) → BIW recruit",
      "car2_me_branch_intro": "Years 0-1 follow this path. Then you choose twice. Each row shows how its pay is worked out (rate × hours, overtime at 1.5×, minus any costs); the running total is just the rows added up.",
      "car2_me_cost": "− {value1} costs",
      "car2_me_cte7": "3 years mobile. Steady customer base. Charging field rates ($85-125/hr, see \"Your own shop\").",
      "car2_me_d1_title": "Decision 1 — age 20: where do you weld next?",
      "car2_me_d2_title": "Decision 2 — age 22: what do you add?",
      "car2_me_formula": "Year pay = rate × 40 h × weeks worked + 1.5 × rate × overtime hours, + side income − costs (tuition, exam fees, equipment). Rates are the middles of the bands this module quotes; per diem (travel lodging money) is not counted as pay. Representative, not a promise.",
      "car2_me_grid_cap": "Total pay by age 26 for every pair of choices from this start (rows: decision 1, columns: decision 2)",
      "car2_me_ndp_co": "ND Paper (Rumford + Old Town mills)",
      "car2_me_ndp_ind": "Paper + pulp",
      "car2_me_ndp_pay": "$30-42/hr (shutdown pay much higher)",
      "car2_me_ndp_what": "Boiler + piping. ASME code work. Hard ticket — pipe welder qual + mill shutdown work.",
      "car2_me_new_cred": "🎓 New: {value1}",
      "car2_me_nopay": "no paid work",
