      "commercial_underwater_welders_earn_80__r2": "Commercial underwater welders earn $80-200K+ but they earn every penny. The work is dangerous, the certifications stack up, and the physics are unforgiving: water cools your weld several times to an order of magnitude faster than air (depending on depth, current and plate), hydrogen from the arc bubble can crack the steel, and the saltwater around you conducts electricity. Two techniques dominate: WET (you and the torch are both in the water) and HYPERBARIC (a sealed dry chamber keeps water out).",
      "cons10_arithmetic": "{value1}% − {value2}% = {value3} percentage points for {value4}.",
