      "cons7_high": "Excessive",
      "cons7_high_aria": "Excessive-flow schematic: shielding gas curls beside the nozzle. Curved dashed pink arrows draw surrounding atmosphere inward toward the pool.",
      "cons7_high_caption": "Excessive flow can become turbulent and draw surrounding atmosphere inward. This is another route to porosity, so increasing flow does not always improve shielding.",
      "cons7_intro": "Select a flow regime to inspect gas coverage around the same torch and joint. Compare how too little and excessive flow can both compromise shielding.",
      "cons7_legend_air": "Pink dots: atmosphere; dashed arrows: inward movement",
      "cons7_legend_gas": "Solid cyan arrows: shielding gas",
      "cons7_legend_pool": "Amber oval: molten pool",
      "cons7_low": "Too little",
      "cons7_low_aria": "Low-flow schematic: a short, partial shielding envelope leaves gaps above the molten pool. Dashed pink arrows point from the surrounding atmosphere toward the pool.",
      "cons7_low_caption": "Insufficient gas flow can leave the pool without enough shielding. The gaps and inward arrows show how surrounding atmosphere can reach it; the concern in this lesson is porosity.",
      "cons7_modes": "Shielding gas flow regime",
      "cons7_note": "Qualitative schematic, not a flow simulation. The regimes do not set a CFH value or predict coverage, defect counts or weld quality for a real setup. Dots and arrows identify atmosphere and gas paths; they are not amounts or particle counts.",
      "cons7_recommended": "Equipment-recommended range",
      "cons7_recommended_aria": "Recommended-range schematic: shielding gas extends from the nozzle to cover the molten pool. Surrounding atmosphere is shown outside the envelope; this does not establish a flow setting.",
      "cons7_recommended_caption": "Use the machine’s recommended range, adjusted for breeze and nozzle distance. The continuous envelope focuses attention on gas coverage around the pool.",
      "cons8_ceriated_gray_r2": "gray",
