      "hunt6_surface": "Surface close-up",
      "hunt6_title": "Committed evidence notebook",
      "hunt6_view_group": "Committed finding evidence views",
      "industry_estimates_put_fatality_rates__r2": "Commercial diving is consistently counted among the most dangerous occupations. There is no single reliable \"times more deadly\" figure for diver-welders - numbers quoted online vary widely and are often unsourced - but the hazards stack: drowning + electric shock + decompression sickness + explosion risk + structural collapse + hypothermia. This isn't a scare tactic - it's why the training is strict and the pay is what it is.",
      "insp10_detail_aria": "Detail of this same weld from {value1} to {value2}, with the gauge at {value3}: {value4}.",
      "insp10_detail_note": "This crop enlarges the same drawing. It follows the gauge and leaves the inspection decision to you.",
      "insp10_detail_window": "Detail window: {value1} to {value2} ({value3} in). Narrow drawing margins keep the gauge visible at the ends.",
      "insp10_hide_detail": "Hide detail at gauge",
      "insp10_position_help": "Move in 1/8 in steps from 0 to {value1}. The overview, arrow controls and this position control move the same gauge.",
      "insp10_position_label": "Gauge start position (in.)",
      "insp10_range_label": "Gauge start position along the weld, in inches",
      "insp10_reading": "At {value1}: {value2}.",
      "insp10_show_detail": "Show detail at gauge",
      "insp10_title": "Place the gauge precisely",
      "insp11_end": "100% · Returned",
      "insp11_identity": "Full trip: 2 × {value1} in = {value2} in. At the cursor: {value3} mm/µs × {value4} µs ÷ 25.4 ≈ {value5} in traversed.",
      "insp11_intro": "Move the manual diagram position from the probe to the flaw and back. The outlined point follows the path in the plate; the dashed cursor follows elapsed time on the complete reference A-scan. This is a diagram position, not a live signal.",
      "insp11_outbound": "Outward leg: probe toward flaw",
