      "metal10_wall": "Pipe wall",
      "metal11_arm_a": "A · Dashed left arm: C − 0.022. Divide this arm by the full 0.748 wt% C span to get the pearlite share at the opposite, right endpoint.",
      "metal11_arm_b": "B · Solid right arm: 0.770 − C. Divide this arm by the same full span to get the proeutectoid ferrite share at the opposite, left endpoint.",
      "metal11_arm_reading": "Opposite arm {value1}: {value2} wt% C.",
      "metal11_carbon": "Overall carbon composition C",
      "metal11_ferrite": "Proeutectoid ferrite (α)",
      "metal11_intro": "Move a separate composition probe through this plain-carbon steel balance just below the eutectoid temperature, after slow equilibrium cooling from austenite. The austenite remaining at the eutectoid composition becomes pearlite; ferrite formed before that reaction is proeutectoid ferrite.",
      "metal11_note": "Pearlite is a constituent made of ferrite and cementite, not a single phase. The ferrite share here counts only ferrite formed before the eutectoid reaction, not the ferrite within pearlite. These endpoint compositions apply at this eutectoid reference, not to ferrite solubility at room temperature. Fractions are rounded to six decimals and percentages to one decimal for display; geometry uses the unrounded values. This reference is independent of the temperature and carbon controls above and does not predict a weld’s final structure, cooling rate or properties.",
      "metal11_pearlite": "Pearlite constituent (P)",
      "metal11_plot_aria": "Composition lever from {value1} to {value2} weight percent carbon, with C at {value3}. Left arm A gives the pearlite share; right arm B gives the proeutectoid ferrite share. The mass-share strip shows {value4}% proeutectoid ferrite and {value5}% pearlite.",
      "metal11_presets": "Lever-rule composition references",
      "metal11_reference": "Reference just below {value1} °C. Composition endpoints: proeutectoid ferrite {value2} wt% C and average pearlite {value3} wt% C.",
      "metal11_share_key": "Mass-share strip: solid = proeutectoid ferrite; hatched = pearlite. The strip groups amounts, not grain shapes or positions.",
      "metal11_source_balance": "Princeton · proeutectoid ferrite and pearlite",
      "metal11_source_princeton": "Princeton · eutectoid endpoint compositions",
      "metal11_sum": "Mass balance: proeutectoid ferrite fraction + pearlite fraction = 1.",
      "metal11_title": "Read the opposite arm: the lever rule",
      "metal11_weighted": "Composition balance: {value1} × {value2} + {value3} × {value4} ≈ {value5} wt% C.",
      "mig_vs_tig_vs_stick_vs_oxy_r2": "MIG, TIG, Stick, flux-core, oxy-fuel, spot",
      "most_weld_cracking_is_martensite_relat_r2": " Hydrogen (cold) cracking in steel usually runs through hard, martensitic HAZ.",
      "only_conductive_materials_depth_limite_r2": "Only conductive materials. Depth is limited by the skin effect: usually a few millimetres or less, and much less in magnetic steel. Surface must be accessible. Calibration sensitive.",
      "paper_mills_sappi_westbrook_verso_pixe_r2": "Paper mills (Sappi Westbrook + Skowhegan, ND Paper Rumford + Old Town), Cianbro (statewide construction), Reed & Reed (large structural), precision manufacturing (IDEXX, Pratt & Whitney).",
