      "pathways_probe_years": "Completed school years: {value1}. Paid work years: {value2}. Annual raise setting: {value3}%.",
      "per_the_wps_on_the_specified_material__r2": "Per the WPS, on the specified material + position. Usually ONE test coupon: the whole weld is visually inspected, then bend specimens are cut from it (or it is radiographed).",
      "pipe10_a": "Wall A · current stacker setting",
      "pipe10_area_ratio": "B ÷ A groove area: {value1}×",
      "pipe10_axes": "Left: wall A. Right: wall B. Both drawings use the same inch scale horizontally and vertically. The root baseline is at the bottom; each grid interval is 1/4 in. The vertical white dimension marks wall thickness.",
      "pipe10_b": "Wall B · comparison only",
      "pipe10_bevel": "Two bevel triangles: ({value1} − 0.0625)² × tan 37.5° = {value2} sq in.",
      "pipe10_inches": "{value1} inches",
      "pipe10_intro": "Compare two prepared grooves at the same scale. The opening rectangle grows with wall thickness; the two bevel triangles grow with the square of the depth above the land. Wall A follows the stacker above. Wall B is a separate comparison.",
      "pipe10_match": "Make B equal A",
      "pipe10_plot_aria": "Prepared groove A is {value1} inches thick; groove B is {value2} inches thick. Both use the same scale, 1/8-inch opening, 1/16-inch land and 37.5-degree bevel per side. Colored regions divide the groove into an opening rectangle and two bevel triangles.",
