      "pipe2_bend_accept": "✓ Accept on this rule: {value1} in. is within the 1/8 in. limit.",
      "pipe2_bend_face": "face bend",
      "pipe2_bend_face_btn": "Face bend",
      "pipe2_bend_face_txt": "The weld FACE (cap side) is on the outside of the bend, so it is stretched. It opens up lack of fusion at the toes and between the top passes, undercut, and porosity near the surface.",
      "pipe2_bend_fails_title": "What fails a bend test",
      "pipe2_bend_group": "Bend specimen type",
      "pipe2_bend_img": "Guided bend test: a {value1} specimen bent into a U around a plunger. The stretched outside surface shows an open discontinuity of {value2} in.; the gauge marks the 1/8 in. limit.",
      "pipe2_bend_intro": "Strips are cut across the test weld, the reinforcement and any backing are ground flush, and each strip is pushed into a U around a plunger. Whatever side ends up on the OUTSIDE of the U is stretched hard, and hidden defects there tear open.",
      "pipe2_bend_lg1": "Grey circle + bar: the plunger. Dark U: the die.",
      "pipe2_bend_lg2": "Orange wedge: the weld. Orange tag: what is on the stretched outside (F face, R root, S side).",
      "pipe2_bend_lg3": "Yellow arrows: tension along the outside surface.",
      "pipe2_bend_lg4": "Panel (×4): the opening against a 1/8 in. gauge; ✓ accept, ✗ reject.",
      "pipe2_bend_plunger": "For common carbon steel the plunger is typically 1-1/2 in. across for a 3/8 in. thick strip; higher-strength metals use a larger plunger. Check the code figure.",
      "pipe2_bend_reject": "✗ Reject: {value1} in. is over the 1/8 in. limit.",
      "pipe2_bend_root": "root bend",
      "pipe2_bend_root_btn": "Root bend",
      "pipe2_bend_root_txt": "The ROOT side is stretched. It opens up incomplete penetration, unfused root edges and suck-back: the root pass is on trial.",
      "pipe2_bend_rule": "D1.1 is commonly cited as rejecting any crack or other open discontinuity over 1/8 in. (3 mm) measured in any direction on the stretched surface. The code also caps the total of the smaller ones and treats corner cracks separately, so verify against the current edition.",
      "pipe2_bend_side": "side bend",
      "pipe2_bend_side_btn": "Side bend",
      "pipe2_bend_side_txt": "A slice cut across the whole weld is bent so a cut face is stretched, putting every pass from root to cap on trial at once. Used on thicker coupons (typically 3/8 in. and up; check the code table).",
      "pipe2_bend_slider": "Largest open discontinuity",
      "pipe2_bend_slider_val": "{value1} in.",
      "pipe2_bend_title": "↩ The guided bend test",
      "pipe2_cell_large": "only on pipe 24 in. OD and up",
