      "pipe_axis_at_45_cannot_rotate_most_dem_r2": "Pipe axis fixed at 45°; the pipe cannot rotate. Every o'clock mixes two positions, so rod angle, body position and travel change continuously. Under AWS D1.1 a 6G groove test qualifies all positions for plate and pipe butt welds (T-, K- and Y-connections need 6GR).",
      "pipe_axis_horizontal_pipe_cannot_rotat_r2": "Pipe axis horizontal and fixed: the pipe cannot rotate. Uphill, the joint is welded in two halves, each from 6 o'clock (bottom) up to 12 o'clock (top). Overhead at 6, vertical at 3 and 9, flat at 12, so technique changes all the way up.",
      "pipeline_welders_typically_earn_40_60__r2": "Pipeline welders typically earn $40-60/hr + per-diem ($100-150/day for housing + meals) + overtime. At $50/hr, 60-hour weeks and $130/day for 26 weeks, that comes to about {value1} before taxes and expenses (worked out below); welders who bring their own welding rig also earn a rig rate. The other side: brutal travel (months from home), physical demands (mostly outdoor + manual), industry cycles (boom/bust with oil prices), + safety risks (heavy equipment, gas, isolation).",
