      "rob10_arm": "Robot arm",
      "rob10_arm_detail": "The arm and its control system are components of the application. The application risk assessment determines the safety functions and settings that are needed.",
      "rob10_assessment": "Assess the complete application during setup and teaching, normal operation, and troubleshooting or maintenance. The assessment considers the arm, tool, workpiece, process and surroundings together.",
      "rob10_caption": "1 · Arm and controls. 2 · Torch. 3 · Workpiece and fixture. 4 · Welding-hazard reference: fume, hazardous light, heat.",
      "rob10_choose": "Application part to inspect",
      "rob10_cobot_intro_r2": "Collaborative robots (\"cobots\") offer safety functions for collaborative applications; the complete application needs a risk assessment to determine its safeguards. Easier to program (often by guiding the arm with your hand to teach positions). Used widely for low-volume welding in small shops that couldn't afford traditional robot cells.",
      "rob10_intro": "Choose a part of the application to see what the assessment includes. The complete application brings the robot, tooling, part and welding process together.",
      "rob10_plan_body_r2": "Application cost and setup effort depend on tooling, integration, training and safeguarding. Experienced welders still help teach and check the welding process.",
      "rob10_plan_title_r2": "Plan the complete application",
      "rob10_process": "Welding process",
      "rob10_process_detail": "Welding adds hazards such as fume, hazardous light, heat and hot surfaces. Robot safety functions do not remove the need to assess these process hazards.",
