      "run_xs_label": "Cross-section: penetration {value1} in. into {value2} in. plate; spec band {value3} to {value4} in.",
      "run_zone_label": "Weld zone. Left and right arrows change travel speed; up and down arrows change amps.",
      "run_zone_review": "Finished bead. Left and right arrows move through it slice by slice.",
      "safe2_banner": "Arc light burns the surface of your eyes in seconds (\"welder's flash\"). Galvanized fume causes metal fume fever. Stainless fume contains hexavalent chromium, a carcinogen. Hot-work sparks fly 35 ft or more and can smolder for hours. Every rule here exists because someone got hurt.",
      "safe2_fig_aria": "Welder figure for the job: {value1}. Wearing: {value2}.",
      "safe2_fig_none": "only a T-shirt and shorts",
      "safe2_fix_breaks": "Fix: schedule short posture breaks every 30-60 minutes during long welds.",
      "safe2_fix_cables": "Fix: add a start-of-shift cable check; tag out and replace any lead with damaged insulation (OSHA 1910.254(d)(9)(iii)).",
      "safe2_fix_clamp": "Fix: clamp the work lead firmly to the part being welded, close to the weld (OSHA 1910.254(d)(2)).",
      "safe2_fix_cyl": "Fix: chain or strap every cylinder upright to a wall or cart, with the valve cap on whenever the regulator is off.",
      "safe2_fix_dry": "Fix: keep spare dry gloves and insulating mats at each station, and keep water off the floor where people weld.",
      "safe2_fix_ext": "Fix: mount a charged ABC extinguisher at each station and train everyone to use it.",
      "safe2_fix_glasses": "Fix: make Z87.1 safety glasses the rule from the shop door on, including under the helmet; slag and chips fly when the hood is up.",
      "safe2_fix_helmet": "Fix: post a shade chart at each station and set every lens to at least the minimum shade for the process and amperage.",
      "safe2_fix_hpa": "Fix: stock earplugs or muffs at every station, where people can grab them without asking.",
      "safe2_fix_hpd": "Fix: provide plugs plus muffs for air-arc gouging and long grinding jobs above about 100 dBA.",
      "safe2_fix_hpr": "Fix: make hearing protection mandatory for grinding, gouging and plasma, and post signs at those stations.",
      "safe2_fix_lev": "Fix: put a fume extractor or downdraft table at each station, with the hood within about 12 in. of the arc (OSHA 1910.252(c)(3)).",
      "safe2_fix_mat": "Fix: put anti-fatigue mats where welders stand, choosing a spark-resistant type near the arc.",
      "safe2_fix_papr": "Fix: set up a respirator program (fit testing, training, medical clearance; OSHA 1910.134) before handing out respirators.",
      "safe2_fix_pos": "Fix: get a positioner, turntable or adjustable stand so the work comes to a comfortable height.",
      "safe2_fix_screens": "Fix: hang welding curtains or screens so no one in an aisle or at a nearby bench has a line of sight to an arc.",
      "safe2_fix_ss": "Fix: capture fume at the source for stainless and galvanized, and have Cr(VI) exposure measured (OSHA 1910.1026).",
      "safe2_fix_watch": "Fix: use a hot-work permit with a trained fire watch during the work and at least 30 minutes after (OSHA); NFPA 51B asks for 60 minutes.",
      "safe2_fp_aria": "Shop floor plan, 100 by 60 ft, with the weld station and its 35-ft hot-work circle. {value1} of 4 combustibles are safe and {value2} of 4 safety items are placed correctly.",
