      "ex_vision_uv_science": "Some reef fish see ultraviolet patterns that humans cannot. UV reflection is different from fluorescence. This screen uses visible colors and cannot show UV itself or recreate an animal’s visual experience.",
      "ex_vision_vivid": "Vivid color",
      "ex_vision_vivid_help": "Richer color for viewing. This artistic enhancement keeps the reef’s depth cues; it does not reveal invisible light.",
      "ex_watch_cleaner": "Watch the cleaning station: fish come by, hold still with their fins spread, and the cleaner picks parasites off their skin, gills and even mouths.",
      "ex_watch_clownfish": "Swim close and watch: anemonefish often duck down into the stinging tentacles, where predators cannot follow.",
      "ex_watch_cots": "See the bright white patch beside it? That is coral it has already eaten: only the white skeleton is left.",
      "ex_watch_label": "Watch for this: ",
      "ex_watch_manta": "Mantas visit cleaning stations too, circling slowly over the reef while cleaner wrasse pick at them.",
      "ex_watch_parrotfish": "Look for the little puffs where it bites the rock: parrotfish grind dead coral and rock into sand.",
      "ex_watch_turtle": "Sea turtles breathe air, so now and then one swims up to the surface for a few breaths and glides back down. A busy turtle in shallow water may come up every minute or two; a resting one can stay down for hours.",
