      "fig_gr_aria": "Cause and effect diagram. Grazing fish eat seaweed and keep space open where young corals can settle. Nutrients from land feed the seaweed, and seaweed crowds out young corals. Below, a marine reserve in the Bahamas where parrotfish were protected: grazing was twice as high as on a fished reef, and seaweed cover was about a quarter as high.",
