      "fig_hb_with": "with the current",
      "fig_hb_without": "without it",
      "fig_hf_aria": "Parts of the Great Barrier Reef in 2022 and 2024. In 2022 they had their highest coral cover in 36 years, much of it fast-growing branching and table corals. In 2024 heat, cyclones and starfish caused the largest one-year drops on record. Recovery is real, and it lasts longest when heatwaves ease.",
      "fig_hf_causes": "after heat, cyclones and starfish",
      "fig_hf_drop": "largest one-year drops on record",
      "fig_hf_ease": "Recovery is real, and it lasts longest when heatwaves ease.",
      "fig_hf_fast": "fast-growing branching and table corals",
      "fig_hf_high": "highest coral cover in 36 years",
      "fig_hf_where": "Parts of the Great Barrier Reef",
      "fig_hg_area": "Most projects cover about a classroom or two.",
      "fig_hg_aria": "Coral gardening in three steps. Small pieces of coral hang on a coral tree nursery, held up off the sand. They grow bigger. Divers plant them on a damaged reef. About two out of three planted corals survive in a typical project, and most projects cover about a classroom or two.",
      "fig_hg_grow": "They grow",
      "fig_hg_nursery": "Pieces in a nursery",
